{"op":"add","path":"/elements/exec_summary","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"Churn intensity differs markedly by plan: Enterprise carries the heaviest burden while Pro carries the lightest, against an overall average of 30.22 per customer (Step 1). Monthly normalized churn is volatile — a 1.28× swing from trough (2024-01) to peak (2024-12) — and the trend direction is increasing, with H2 averaging 15.4% different from H1 (Step 2). Crucially, high-churn months are not explained by a lower-ARPU customer mix; they coincide with elevated new MRR, expansion MRR, and customer volume — indicating churn amplifies alongside growth rather than reflecting pricing pressure (Step 3).","variant":"insight"},"children":[]}}
